+- **Test classes that start a tool under a hard time limit share one xunit collection (experiment; card 368 retro, Decider D247).** While this entry is on trial: an acceptance test class that starts the bench tools or another external process under a hard time limit (for example the 20 second limit of the bench timeout test) carries `[Collection("Bench processes")]`, so that two such classes never overlap in one full run; the independent gate reviewer checks every new class of that kind and records it in its review; the classes CSharpBaselineAcceptance and PrivateHoldoutResults, which still overlap, join the collection in the bug filed with this pick.
+  - Hypothesis: a time-limited test that never competes with another process-starting class stops failing under load. Metric: sign-off attempts per card (card 368: 2, the first failed on the timing test in two of four full runs), target 1, and full-suite timing failures, target 0. Counter-metric: minutes per full suite (card 368: about 10) and the seconds the serial collection adds. Trial: the next 3 cards that add or touch a test class that starts the bench tools or another external process, counted from Decider D247. Owner: the facilitator. Review at the third card's retro: keep, change or remove.
